@sarahwiegreffe I agree. While OpenAI doesn't like talking about exact model sizes / parameter counts anymore, documentation should definitely be better.

text-davinci-002 isn't the model from the InstructGPT paper. The closest to the paper is text-davinciplus-002.

https://t.co/LDo507M2yG

@Raza_Habib496 I don't know of any methods that can scale to proofs about large language models unfortunately.

Agreed that reward uncertainty would be great to have, but I haven't seen anything that works at scale yet.

Not convinced that it's necessary or sufficient for safe interruptibility.

@annnnhe (a) iirc it was 3 functions with one subtle bug each, so only a small fraction of tokens
(b) good idea! It should help a bit but I'd be surprised if it solved the problem
(c) probably! I expect that Codex "knows" the code is buggy for our examples some of the time.
